 "article": {
  "title": "Learning a Language by Living It",
  "topic": "教育（沉浸式语言学习）",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "words": 172,
  "paras": [
   "Most adults who study a foreign language for years still freeze when a waiter speaks quickly. The problem is rarely vocabulary. It is that classrooms teach language as a subject rather than as a tool.",
   "Teachers who take students outside the room report a different pattern. A student who has to buy a ticket, ask for a receipt and complain about a delay learns three structures in an hour, because those structures were the only way to get what she wanted.",
   "Immersion has costs. It is exhausting, it produces mistakes, and it can humiliate an adult who is used to being competent. Good programmes build in a safe hour at the end of the day, when learners can ask questions in their own language and recover.",
   "The practical advice is modest. Choose one weekly activity you already enjoy and do it in the new language: cook from a foreign recipe, follow a football commentary, listen to a podcast about a subject you know well. Comprehension grows fastest where curiosity is already present."
  ],
  "zh": "许多学了多年外语的成年人，一遇到服务员语速快就僵住。问题很少出在词汇量，而在于课堂把语言当成一门学科，而不是一件工具。把学生带出教室的老师看到的是另一种情形：一个必须自己买票、要发票、为晚点投诉的学生，一小时里就学会了三种句型，因为那几种句型是她拿到想要东西的唯一途径。沉浸也有代价：累、会出错，还会让习惯了自己很能干的成年人感到丢脸。好的项目会在一天结束时留出一小时“安全时间”，让学习者用母语提问、缓过来。可操作的建议很朴素：挑一件你本来就喜欢的每周活动，用外语去做——照外文菜谱做饭、听球赛解说、听你熟悉领域的播客。理解力总是在好奇心已经存在的地方长得最快。",
  "hard": [
   {
    "en": "It is that classrooms teach language as a subject rather than as a tool.",
    "cn": "问题在于课堂把语言当作一门学科来教，而不是当作工具。",
    "why": "It is that … 是强调句的省略形式（强调原因）；rather than 连接两个 as 短语，表示取舍而非并列，注意其后用名词或动名词。"
   },
   {
    "en": "A student who has to buy a ticket, ask for a receipt and complain about a delay learns three structures in an hour.",
    "cn": "一个必须买票、要发票、为晚点投诉的学生，一小时内就学会了三种句型。",
    "why": "主语带较长的 who 定语从句，三个不定式并列，真正谓语 learns 在后面；写作时先给主语再给动作，句子会显得有分量。"
   }
  ],
